        <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Two Not Touch is the classic American puzzle-book name for the same game — it describes the rule that two stars may not touch, even diagonally. Star Battle is the modern name used by apps and puzzle sites. Same rules, same grids, two names. GridPaw is not affiliated with any official publisher.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Are star battle puzzles good for your brain?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Star Battle trains spatial reasoning, planning and pure logic, with no arithmetic and no vocabulary — just the structure of the board. Puzzle publishers routinely describe it as excellent brain training for all ages, from kids to lifelong solver fans.</div>
      </details>
